  "title": "merge: Don't abort a merge on a short read",
  "description": "If the error reading a capture file during a merge is\nWTAP_ERR_SHORT_READ, that's a fatal error as far as reading from\n_that_ file, but it doesn't mean we have to abort the entire merge.\nIt's a relatively normal condition from truncated files.\n\nReport the error, stop processing that file, but keep going with the\nmerge.\n\nFix #15379 (at least the example shown there; we might want to\nkeep on trucking through WTAP_ERR_BAD_FILE too.)",
